# Notation ratchet (PR #1188, R1188-U6 and R1188-U7;
# docs/links-notation-style.md).
#
# The ceilings on the links notation we own, per scope of
# data/meta/notation-rules.lino, measured by scripts/measure-notation.mjs
# (gate check-notation). Each count is of distinct items, so a new record
# that reuses existing keys moves nothing, while a new `_` name, a new
# abbreviated name, a new duplicated block or a new repeated field raises a
# count and fails the gate. The ceilings only fall: `--write` lowers them to
# the measure after a rule pass. `characters` is recorded for the concise-form
# passes and is not a ceiling, since new seed data rightly adds characters.
#
# History. On 2026-10-08 the seed-lexemes family wrote 4916 lexemes in the
# concise form (`lexeme en "read" "open"` with the fields its surfaces share
# below it): data/seed fell from 3,532,300 to 3,150,411 characters and its
# duplicated blocks from 45 to 27. Its repeated fields were re-based from 115
# to 184 by the same change, not by new repetition: a field every surface of a
# lexeme shares (`part_of_speech noun`) now sits once on the lexeme, where the
# measure sees the same field on the sibling lexemes of other languages. That
# is the next deduplication: state it once on the meaning.
notation-ratchet
  scope data/meta
    underscore-names 2867
    abbreviated-names 200
    duplicated-blocks 9
    repeated-fields 84
    characters 1707426
  scope data/seed
    underscore-names 9419
    abbreviated-names 245
    duplicated-blocks 27
    repeated-fields 184
    characters 3150411
